ing on a grid edge (bottom row in both training pairs). The output keeps the blobs mostly intact, but a striped \"ladder\" grows out of the yellow bar across the whole grid, and some rows of the blobs turn green (3).\n\n## Reading the pattern from the yellow bar outward\n\nLooking at pair 1 from the bar (row 28) upward:\n\n- row 28: `4` bar (the original)\n- row 27: background only\n- row 26: `4` bar at the same columns — overwriting blob cells there\n- row 25: background at the bar's columns — blob cells there are erased to 1\n- row 24: a `3` row: the whole row's blob cells turn 3, and the bar's columns are 3 too\n- row 23: background at the bar's columns\n- row 22: `4` again, and the cycle restarts.\n\nSo, measured by distance `d` from the bar, the pattern has period 6: `4, blank, 4, blank, 3-full-row, blank`. \"Blank\" means the bar's span is forced to background even if a blob occupied it (that is the `8->1` and `2->8` transitions in the fact sheet). The `3` lines explain the long horizontal green segments like (18,2)->(18,17) in pair 1: those are blob rows at distance 4 mod 6 recoloured wholesale, plus the bar span itself in green even where there was no blob (e.g. row 0 of pair 1). The ladder runs until it hits the opposite edge.\n\nThe fact sheet warns the test sizes differ from training, so nothing may be tied to absolute row numbers — everything is measured from the bar, stepping away from the edge the bar touches. Test 1 has the bar on the top row (so the ladder grows downward), and test 2 has a vertical bar in column 0 (so the ladder grows rightward, with \"rows\" becoming columns). The program detects orientation from the bar: if all its cells share one row it's horizontal, otherwise vertical; the step direction is +1 if the bar sits at index 0 and −1 otherwise.\n\n## Construction\n\n1. Start from the input canvas.\n2. For each distance `d = 0, 1, 2, ...` from the bar, pick the line at that distance and apply `d mod 6`:\n   - 0 or 2 → paint the bar's span 4;\n   - 1, 3, 5 → paint the bar's span background;\n   - 4 → recolour every non-background cell of that line to 3, and paint the bar's span 3.\n3. Stop at the far edge. I emit a checkpoint after each completed 6-line cycle so a learner can watch the ladder climb, then emit the finished grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    ys, xs = np.where(g == 4)\n    out = g.copy()\n    emit(out, \"Start from the input: blobs plus a single yellow (4) bar on one edge; the ladder will grow from that bar.\")\n\n    horizontal = len(set(ys.tolist())) == 1\n    if horizontal:\n        start = ys[0]\n        step = 1 if start == 0 else -1\n        lo, hi = xs.min(), xs.max()\n        n = H\n    else:\n        start = xs[0]\n        step = 1 if start == 0 else -1\n        lo, hi = ys.min(), ys.max()\n        n = W\n\n    def paint(idx, m):\n        if horizontal:\n            if m % 2 == 1:\n                out[idx, lo:hi+1] = bg\n            elif m == 4:\n                out[idx, g[idx] != bg] = 3\n                out[idx, lo:hi+1] = 3\n            else:\n                out[idx, lo:hi+1] = 4\n        else:\n            if m % 2 == 1:\n                out[lo:hi+1, idx] = bg\n            elif m == 4:\n                out[g[:, idx] != bg, idx] = 3\n                out[lo:hi+1, idx] = 3\n            else:\n                out[lo:hi+1, idx] = 4\n\n    for d in range(n):\n        idx = start + d * step\n        if not (0 <= idx < n):\n            break\n        m = d % 6\n        paint(idx, m)\n        if m == 5:\n            emit(out, f\"Completed one 6-line cycle at distance {d} from the bar: 4, blank, 4, blank, full green (3) line, blank.\")\n\n    emit(out, \"Ladder reaches the far edge: final result.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"g horizontal green segments like (18,2)->(18,17) in pair 1: those are blob rows at distance 4 mod 6 recoloured wholesale, plus the bar span itself in green even where there was no blob (e.g. row 0 of pair 1)."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- 4 → recolour every non-background cell of that line to 3, and paint the bar's span 3."}],"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So, measured by distance `d` from the bar, the pattern has period 6: `4, blank, 4, blank, 3-full-row, blank`. \"Blank\" means the bar's span is forced to background even if a blob occupied it (that is the `8->1` and `2->8` transitions in the fact sheet)."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"2eb97a9c7d033378ddc11cfb91fa00f2e900eade62520af8df3001a4c1e7c4b5","task_sha256":"480a21439b30632465d24d4de58353dbaaa5a44ad92a590e0ad05f5e56326163","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
